EXIT_CODES having only a SUCCESS member is authoritative for createAntigravityTransport's finalize() hardcoding exitCode: EXIT_CODES.SUCCESS on every branch, since Antigravity has no exit-code signaling channel at all; adding an ERROR or BLOCK member to EXIT_CODES without updating every finalize() branch would silently reintroduce a channel the wire contract says does not exist. The 'Wire fundamentals' conformance block is the only check that would catch such drift, by asserting exit code 0 across every outcome kind.
